Negative control for a scene that THREW being said out loud (`S14` · `R6-13`).

Takes the failure chip off the bar and leaves everything else — the player still
catches the throw, still holds the reason, still flips to `FAILED` — so the only
claim that can go red is the ruled one: a failed arm or a refused assertion is
reported where the hand that pressed the control is looking. Without it the only
trace is a bar that has quietly stopped moving, which reads as a dead control.

Re-targeted 2026-08-13 after the `R7-10`/`R7-8` restructure: the hunk's context
moved when the bar grew its controls row and its rail row. Same claim, same red,
current source.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the scene-failure case — a player holding a failure renders it on the bar,
with the thrower's own sentence.

